# Next Car in the pause menu

Single Race, Practice, Stunt Arena, and Time Trial expose a Next Car row directly
after Next Track. The value starts at the current car. Left/right cycles through
valid, player-selectable cars in the runtime pool and wraps at either end;
confirm restarts the current level with that car and its default skin. Browsing
does not change the current car until confirmed. Confirming the current car
restarts without changing its skin. The row remains available when only the
current car is eligible. Championship, multiplayer, replays, and other race modes
retain their native menus.

The implementation lives in MenuMod.cpp. It hooks the native pause-menu builder
at 0x00542ed0 and action handler at 0x00542c70, copies the Next Track row template
at 0x006634c0, and borrows locale slot 0x28 only while displaying the custom row.
The native pause menu may ignore Cancel, so the label is restored only when the
panel leaves or before the next build.

Confirm queues the selected model, disables the current session's
random-car/random-track flags, and uses the native immediate
restart path: write 6 through the request pointer at 0x006a65e0, close the menu,
and call SetRaceState(3) at 0x0048a560. After Race_TeardownAndSave saves the old
session/replay, its hook applies the pending model/default skin and names to the
first cached participant at PlayerRaceInfo + 0x50, plus RaceSettings and
GameModeRuntime::playerModelId (+0x0C). Solo restarts reuse that participant
table rather than calling RaceSessionSetup.
LevelLoad then creates the new car normally. The selector is a release feature
and does not depend on the temporary Practice-star-reset hack.

For a changed car in Single Race, ApplyPendingInRaceCarSelection also calls
RandomizeCarPicks (0x0044fb30) after updating RaceSettings. The native routine
uses RaceSettings::playerModelIds to exclude local players' cars and choose CPU
cars from the player's rating, falling back to lower ratings when needed. It
updates CPU model IDs, names, and skins in the cached participant table. Normal
Single Race setup calls it at 0x0045165d, before AssignStartPositions
(0x0044f980). Its selected-car buffer holds sixteen entries, so the refresh caps
the cached participant count at sixteen, clears the thirty-car cache, then uses
Hook_AssignStartPositions to expand and position the rebuilt roster normally.
The expansion's duplicate fallback pool also excludes the player model, matching
native picks when a rating has fewer unique CPU cars than the requested grid.
An unchanged selection returns before this refresh and retains its opponents.

Time Trial resource loading at 0x004557e0 uses the rating of the cached
GameModeRuntime::playerModelId to select its table. LoadTrackLeaderboards
(0x004765f0) loads the tables and SelectTrackLeaderboard (0x00476070) selects
the requested rating, or merges ratings for Global mode. InitializeRaceSession
then calls LoadLocalTimeTrialGhost (0x0044dba0) and
LoadDownloadedTimeTrialGhost (0x0044ea60), which use the same cached car in
Per-Rating mode. Updating only the participant and RaceSettings leaves both
the table and ghost on the previous rating. Updating the cached ID after
teardown lets the native restart reload both for the new car.

Build Debug and Release with the existing CMake randomizer target. The local
build/next_car_live.py smoke test uses a copied, isolated profile and exercises
the native menu and keyboard path, left/right selection, resuming without
applying a choice, keeping the track, and repeated car switches.

The local build/time_trial_next_car_live.py regression test uses copied times
and an isolated preference directory. It checks the cached model, selected
per-rating table, and loaded ghost rating when switching between ratings,
switching back, and restarting with the same car.

The local build/single_race_next_car_live.py regression test accepts a car count
(8 or 30) and checks switching to an existing CPU car, cross-rating picks,
opponent names, unchanged track/laps, repeated switches, and retaining the
roster and skins when the same car is confirmed, using an isolated profile.
